#: ImplementationTwoGroups.md:1
msgid "Premise"
msgstr "前提"

#: ImplementationTwoGroups.md:3
msgid ""
"We now try to change what we made in the [self-"
"coordination](Implementation.md) and determine the coordination between two "
"groups."
msgstr "[Self-coordination](Implementation.md) を変更し、2 Group 間を計算します。"

#: ImplementationTwoGroups.md:5
msgid ""
"I am assuming that you have already read the details about how the "
"coordination is implemented in the [other chapter](Implementation.md). So "
"here you will see some more abstract pseudo code. Always refer to my "
"(evolving) [repository](https://github.com/Iximiel/cudaOnPlumed) and on the "
"main [plumed repository](https://github.com/plumed/plumed2) for a more "
"accurate and performant code."
msgstr ""
"[前の章](Implementation.md) を読んでいる前提で、抽象的な疑似コードを示します。正確で高速なコードは、更新中の "
"[リポジトリ](https://github.com/Iximiel/cudaOnPlumed) と [PLUMED "
"本体](https://github.com/plumed/plumed2) を参照してください。"

#: ImplementationTwoGroups.md:8
msgid "Wait, and the derivatives?"
msgstr "微分はどうするか"

#: ImplementationTwoGroups.md:9
msgid ""
"First of all let's hastily rewrite the core kernel, stripped of the "
"declarations"
msgstr "宣言を除き、主要 Kernel を書き直します。"

#: ImplementationTwoGroups.md:69
msgid ""
"We want the coordination between all of the atoms of 'GROUPA' and all of the"
" atoms of 'GROUPB'. But this kernel solves a different problem: it loops on "
"ALL the atoms and calculates the coordination between ALL of them."
msgstr ""
"目的は GROUPA の全原子と GROUPB の全原子の間の Coordination ですが、この Kernel は全原子間を計算してしまいます。"

#: ImplementationTwoGroups.md:72
msgid "How can we work around this?"
msgstr "どう回避しますか？"

#: ImplementationTwoGroups.md:74
msgid ""
"Let's start to acknowledge that we will need to have different specialized "
"kernels (since branching within a kernel will generate a loss of "
"performance)."
msgstr "Kernel 内の分岐は性能を落とすため、別々の専用 Kernel が必要です。"

#: ImplementationTwoGroups.md:76
msgid "Then we change the signature of the new kernel:"
msgstr "新しい Kernel の Signature を変えます。"

#: ImplementationTwoGroups.md:87
msgid "So that we pass the parameters of the two groups separately."
msgstr "2 Group のパラメータを別々に渡します。"

#: ImplementationTwoGroups.md:89
msgid "we then make the first part of the kernel around this change ()"
msgstr "変更に合わせて Kernel の先頭を作ります。()"

#: ImplementationTwoGroups.md:108
msgid ""
"So now each atom of group A will ONLY interact with the atoms in group B, "
"then we rewrote the core of the loop, discarding the \"triangular things\" "
"of before:"
msgstr "Group A の各原子は Group B のみと相互作用します。前の三角形部分を除き、Loop の中心を書き直します。"

#: ImplementationTwoGroups.md:140
msgid "And we end the kernel exactly like in the single group case:"
msgstr "終わりは1 Group の場合と同じです。"

#: ImplementationTwoGroups.md:158
msgid ""
"But now we still miss a piece: atoms indexed `i` are in GROUPA: it looks "
"like we are storing the derivatives the coordination and the virial only "
"relative to one of the two groups. This affirmation is true only about the "
"derivatives since coordination and virial are \"couple\" properties."
msgstr ""
"まだ不足があります。`i` は GROUPA なので、片方の微分・Coordination・Virial しか保存していないように見えます。ただし "
"Coordination と Virial は Pair の量なので、問題は微分だけです。"

#: ImplementationTwoGroups.md:161
msgid ""
"So, how do we solve this new problem of getting the derivatives of GROUPB?"
msgstr "GROUPB の微分はどう求めますか？"

#: ImplementationTwoGroups.md:163
msgid "Calculationg the derivatives of the atoms B"
msgstr "Group B 原子の微分計算"

#: ImplementationTwoGroups.md:165
msgid ""
"We might calculate the derivative for group B along the ones of group A, but"
" we will end up needing `size`(groupA) * size(groupB)` extra triplette of "
"floats to be stored during the execution of the first kernel because we "
"can't sum on the same piece of data unless we stop the parallel calculation "
"to avoid a data race. Ad with this solution we would need to store these "
"values since we are traversing the \"matrix of couples\" along the \"group A"
" axis\"."
msgstr ""
"A と同時に B の微分も計算できますが、最初の Kernel で `size`(groupA) * size(groupB)` 個の Float "
"3つ組を余分に保存する必要があります。同じデータへの加算は Data Race を防ぐため並列計算を止める必要があり、Pair Matrix の A "
"軸方向に進むので値の保存が必要です。"

#: ImplementationTwoGroups.md:171
msgid ""
"But in that case, we will need `size(groupA) * size(groupB) * 8` bytes of "
"memory for each dimension (3 in our case). That means, for example, that for"
" a system of 10000 atoms, in two groups of 5000 will be 200000000 bytes, "
"that are roughly 200 MB, but since the relationship is quadratic and the "
"memory on a GPU is usually scarce, is not a scalable option (with a group of"
" 100000 atoms divide d in two would be 20GB)."
msgstr ""
"各次元（3次元）に `size(groupA) * size(groupB) * 8` Byte "
"が必要です。10000原子を5000ずつにすると200000000 Byte、約200 MB です。二乗で増え、GPU Memory は限られるため "
"Scalable ではありません。100000原子を半分ずつなら20 GB です。"

#: ImplementationTwoGroups.md:176
msgid ""
"The easiest solution that I found is to redo the same loop, but with "
"inverted groups, but keeping ONLY calculating only the derivatives. This "
"does not make the algorithm scale differently (summing two algorithms with "
"the same time complexity is an algorithm with the same time complexity) and "
"does not use extra space."
msgstr ""
"最も簡単なのは、Group を入れ替えて同じ Loop を再実行し、微分だけ計算することです。同じ Time Complexity の計算を足しても "
"Complexity は変わらず、追加領域も不要です。"

#: ImplementationTwoGroups.md:233
msgid "Remarks"
msgstr "補足"

#: ImplementationTwoGroups.md:234
msgid ""
"The problem of this approach is that if there is a great imbalance in "
"numbers between the two groups, written as is does not scale efficiently."
msgstr "Group 間の原子数が大きく異なる場合、この実装は効率が悪くなります。"

#: ImplementationTwoGroups.md:237
msgid ""
"For example, if you have group A with 1000 atoms and b with only one, you "
"will get the first kernel doing a single iteration in 1000 threads for the "
"first atoms, and the second kernel occupying a single thread for 1000 "
"iterations. But this may be solved by trying to balance how much work each "
"thread will need to do."
msgstr ""
"例えば A が1000原子、B が1個なら、最初は1000 Thread が1回ずつ、次は1 Thread が1000回処理します。各 Thread "
"の負荷を均等にすれば改善できます。"
